      "message": "p2p: don't add already-known transactions to the reject filter\n\nTX_CONFLICT means the transaction is already known, in the mempool or\nconfirmed, not that it is invalid. Its wtxid still went into the reject\nfilter. For a witnessless copy that is also the txid, so if the known\nparent then left the mempool before the next block, a child arriving\nafterwards was dropped as having a rejected parent. For the honest\nversion of a parent whose other-witness version is in the mempool, the\nhonest parent itself was ignored once that version left.\n\nDon't add TX_CONFLICT results to the reject filter. The entry only saved\nre-downloading and re-checking a transaction we already have.\n\nThis also keeps a witnessless copy of a confirmed transaction out of\nthe filter, as it is rejected as already known when one of its outputs\nis in the coins cache, so children spending that transaction are no\nlonger dropped. A copy of a coinbase is rejected as TX_CONSENSUS\ninstead, before any input lookup, and still poisons the coinbase's\ntxid.\n\nUpdate the rejection-type table for TX_CONFLICT. In the liveness\ntarget, remove the replayed-parent hole and narrow the stripped\nconfirmed-parent hole to children funded by a coinbase.",
